    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d905">

                <pb facs="0815" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/468</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Commission for Relief in
                        Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York, N. Y.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 24, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>We this morning received word from London that British Government had issued
                    safe-conduct to ships around northern route, and we anticipate that master,
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Olaf Kyrre</hi> will receive his pass
                    immediately. We have requested British Ambassador, Washington to expedite
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert Hoover</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
